<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico's 28-day Cetes seen up sharply.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico's 28-day Cetes seen up sharply.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's bellwether 28-day cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 147 basis points to 20.77 percent, and rates are also seen rising at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM     LAST WEEK     THIS WEEK'S SURVEY     CHANGE</p>
<p>   28-DAY    19.30		20.77		  +147 bps</p>
<p>   91-DAY    21.31		21.70		   +39 bps</p>
<p>  182-DAY    21.99		22.12		   +13 bps</p>
<p>  343-DAY    22.92		22.98		    +6 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 local time/2200 GMT.</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9565))</p>
